<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:25:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>对于先前接受过放射治疗的脑转移瘤，手术的价值是三倍</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/the-threefold-value-of-surgery-in-previously-irradiated-brain-metastases</link><description>在先前接受过辐射的脑转移瘤 (BM) 中区分放射性坏死 (RN) 和肿瘤复发 (TR) 仍然是一个挑战。成像技术缺乏足够的诊断可靠性，而两个实体之间的治疗意义不同。本研究旨在评估手术对进行性辐照骨髓瘤患者的诊断、治疗和预后价值。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/the-threefold-value-of-surgery-in-previously-irradiated-brain-metastases.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/the-threefold-value-of-surgery-in-previously-irradiated-brain-metastases</guid></item><item><title>摘要： 1 肿瘤学研究和</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/abstract-1-division-of-oncology-research-and</link><description>1&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/abstract163.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/abstract-1-division-of-oncology-research-and</guid></item><item><title>临床 CAR T 细胞活性的基因组相关性</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/genomic-correlates-of-clinical-car-t-cell-activity</link><description>种系变异&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/genomic-correlates-of-clinical-car-t-cell-activity2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:54:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/genomic-correlates-of-clinical-car-t-cell-activity</guid></item><item><title>导致疾病的基因缺失后，脑细胞如何恢复健康生长和连接</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/how-brain-cells-restore-healthy-growth-and-connections-after-a-disease-causing-genetic-deletion</link><description>弗吉尼亚理工大学弗拉林生物医学研究所的科学家们发现了一种实验疗法如何帮助脑细胞克服致病基因缺失的影响。该疗法不是修复缺失及其直接后果，而是通过帮助有风险的神经元更正常地生长和连接来改变大脑发育方向。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/how-brain-cells-restore-healthy-growth-and-connections-after-a-disease-causing-genetic-deletion.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:39:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/how-brain-cells-restore-healthy-growth-and-connections-after-a-disease-causing-genetic-deletion</guid></item><item><title>较高的维生素 A 水平与患有哮喘的儿童和成人更好的肺功能有关</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/higher-vitamin-a-levels-linked-to-better-lung-function-in-children-and-adults-with-asthma</link><description>维生素 A 与改善患有哮喘的儿童和成人的肺功能有关；然而，维生素 D 仅对成人显示出相同的益处。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/higher-vitamin-a-levels-linked-to-better-lung-function-in-children-and-adults-with-asthma.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/higher-vitamin-a-levels-linked-to-better-lung-function-in-children-and-adults-with-asthma</guid></item><item><title>我们发现了迄今为止最好的巨大游荡黑洞的例子</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/weve-found-the-best-example-yet-of-an-enormous-wandering-black-hole</link><description>天文学家利用一颗被撕裂的恒星发出的光，发现了一个远离银河系中心的超大质量黑洞&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/weve-found-the-best-example-yet-of-an-enormous-wandering-black-hole2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/weve-found-the-best-example-yet-of-an-enormous-wandering-black-hole</guid></item><item><title>单个贴片合并多个生理信号，以实现更简单的健康监测</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/single-patch-merges-multiple-physiological-signals-for-simpler-health-monitoring</link><description>可穿戴健康监测器的功能越来越强大，但大多数仍然受到以下事实的限制：跟踪不同类型的身体信号需要单独的传感器，每个传感器都有自己的电路和皮肤块。这导致设备体积更大、功耗更高，并且给需要全天候监控的人带来更大的不适。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/single-patch-merges-multiple-physiological-signals-for-simpler-health-monitoring2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:54:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/single-patch-merges-multiple-physiological-signals-for-simpler-health-monitoring</guid></item><item><title>植物聚合物木质素显示出未来骨再生的希望</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/plant-polymer-lignin-shows-promise-for-future-bone-regeneration</link><description>一项新的研究表明，木质素（一种天然植物聚合物）可以转化为一种生物活性材料，促进类骨矿物质的形成，同时支持成骨细胞的生长。受植物中木质素和二氧化硅之间自然伙伴关系的启发，该研究为未来骨再生疗法的可持续植物基材料迈出了有希望的一步。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/plant-polymer-lignin-shows-promise-for-future-bone-regeneration.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:39:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/plant-polymer-lignin-shows-promise-for-future-bone-regeneration</guid></item><item><title>RAMPC 将国内 18A 生产交给战争部，英特尔成为美国唯一领先的芯片制造商</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/intel-emerges-as-americas-only-leadingedge-chipmaker-as-rampc-hands-the-department-of-war-domestic-18a-production</link><description>英特尔已完成其&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/intel-emerges-as-americas-only-leadingedge-chipmaker-as-rampc-hands-the-department-of-war-domestic-18a-production.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:24:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/intel-emerges-as-americas-only-leadingedge-chipmaker-as-rampc-hands-the-department-of-war-domestic-18a-production</guid></item><item><title>新研究表明“热电子”如何在十亿分之一秒内重塑金属</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/new-research-shows-how-hot-electrons-can-reshape-metals-in-billionths-of-a-second</link><description>曼彻斯特大学的研究人员揭示了强烈的电子激发如何在不加热原子晶格的情况下触发金属的快速结构变化，为超快材料行为提供了新的见解。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-research-shows-how-hot-electrons-can-reshape-metals-in-billionths-of-a-second2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:09:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/new-research-shows-how-hot-electrons-can-reshape-metals-in-billionths-of-a-second</guid></item></channel></rss>